WEBVTT

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.150
Vice Abbot...

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.370
Residents of Nanzenji Temple:
I have taken the dragon.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.500
I swear... What's goin' on here?

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.620
I can't believe they're so sophisticated.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.370
I'm shocked.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.780
Um, could I ask what's going on?

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:30.880
Aoi-san...

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.740
The owner and I recently visited 
several art museums.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.390
We found impostors mixed 
in among the exhibits.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.390
Impostors?

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.270
Just what it sounds like.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.520
Counterfeits.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.150
Counterfeits?

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:05.100
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.240
Episode 5

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.240
"The Lost Dragon"

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.620
Counterfeits?

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.250
I saw one when I first 
started working here...

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.720
Holmes-san, you saw through it immediately,

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.130
and turned the man away, right?

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.440
Yes.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:37.760
But the counterfeits we saw this 
time were quite sophisticated.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:44.000
It's deplorable, seein' fakes like 
those right on display in a museum.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.220
It's almost as if they're 
testing appraisers like us.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.840
That's the impression I got of the maker.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.770
Testing... appraisers?

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:58.430
Look, the people who counterfeit art
 are experts in their own way.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:01.870
We appraisers gotta stay one step ahead.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:05.000
We need you to up your game, too.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.410
I understand.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.790
Now, let's see...

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:11.310
I'm gonna drop in on Yanagihara-han.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.770
Don't forget about tomorrow!

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:16.050
Of course. Although, I must say...

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:17.800
Yeah?

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.320
You don't need to put up a front for me.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.930
You're going to Pontocho 
to have fun, aren't you?

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:28.310
Shut up! That's how I stay 
healthy and energetic!

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.940
The owner never changes, does he?

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:38.440
Heya!

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.440
If it isn't Akihito-san.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.400
I came all the way from Tokyo to stop by,

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.560
but now I feel like a third wheel.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.140
Really?

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.350
I believe you came here to act in 
a television program set in Kyoto,

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:55.080
and you've come here to 
get information from me.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.500
H-How did you know all that?!

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:02.480
Someone like you 
who has no interest in antiques

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:05.090
would never visit Kyoto midsummer, 
much less our store,

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:07.470
unless you needed help with work.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:11.040
Boy, you're Holmes through and through.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.490
You hit the nail on the head.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:17.230
I've been cast as the navigator for an 
upcoming travel show called <i>Kyoto Days</i>.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.080
Wow!

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.930
For the first episode, I'm supposed 
to show off Nanzenji Temple,

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:23.610
but I don't know it too well.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.700
So I was thinking, maybe 
Holmes would be willing to...

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.030
Absolutely not.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.490
At least let me finish!

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.000
<i>There's Holmes-san's trademark nastiness...</i>

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.580
What's the big deal?

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.910
I bet you know tons about it.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:39.640
Couldn't you learn enough 
from books and the internet?

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.330
It's not like that!

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.010
What is it like, then?

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:48.950
That stuff you told me about my inheritance
 from Dad actually stuck with me!

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.140
The way you talk is special!

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:54.520
So please! Come with me to Nanzenji!

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:56.270
Very well.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.770
You mean it?!

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:02.110
I would be hard-pressed to refuse 
when you're so insistent.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.340
It may be sudden, but would 
tomorrow be acceptable?

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:07.050
I'm okay with that, but...

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:08.780
Aoi-chan, want to come along?

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:12.660
Oh, no... I'll be watching 
the store all day tomorrow.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:17.000
The truth is, I have an engagement at 
Nanzenji Temple tomorrow afternoon anyway.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.420
So you already had business there, huh?

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.270
Is that what the owner mentioned earlier?

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:24.920
Yes. It's not for an appraisal,

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:27.300
but it sounds like a rather difficult matter.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.010
I see...

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.330
Well, sorry, Aoi-chan!

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.800
Guess I'll be borrowing Holmes tomorrow!

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:38.560
Now, if you could peruse 
these documents beforehand...

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:41.570
All those?!

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.170
<i>That's Holmes-san for you...</i>

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.690
<i>So nasty.</i>

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.800
Awesome!

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:54.450
Yes.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:58.370
It makes you want to shout, 
"Such a view, such a view!"

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.800
That's Ishikawa Goemon, right?

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:04.160
I can't believe the world's greatest 
thief climbed up here too!

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.120
He didn't, actually.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.840
That's from a kabuki play.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:14.080
This gate wasn't built until after the 
historical Ishikawa Goemon's execution.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.850
Aw, really?

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:22.110
It just shows the spirit of adventure the
 people of Kyoto felt when they saw this view.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.460
I get it.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.490
It sure is a crazy awesome view!

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.420
Akihito-san.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:31.850
That honest enthusiasm 
of yours is your best trait.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:35.540
You should convey that sense 
of wonder to the viewers.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:42.150
But please refrain from 
saying things like "crazy awesome."

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:46.220
You'll be representing Kyoto men
 in this program, after all.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.100
I know that!

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:51.760
Anyway, let's see the aqueduct.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.640
Awesome! I never knew there 
was a bridge this close by!

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:59.520
The aqueduct was built in the Meiji era.

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:04.650
Water from Lake Biwa flows 
like a stream over the bridge.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:12.540
By the way, do you have a girlfriend?

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:13.660
I do not.

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:17.040
I bet you meet plenty of girls, though.

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:22.170
When I'm with someone, I quickly 
learn a great deal about them.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:26.780
When they're lying, 
when they're being calculating...

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:29.030
I see too much of all of it.

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:30.300
Huh...

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:35.300
And the first person I ever dated 
rewarded me with painful betrayal.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.930
It's put me off of women completely.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:47.190
At the moment, I'd much prefer 
superficial, temporary liaisons.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:51.450
<i>Wow, that's a pretty major 
thing he just put out there...</i>

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:55.420
Of course, I know that's hardly acceptable, 
so please don't tell anyone I said it.

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:56.700
S-Sure...

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:02.080
Hey, what about Aoi-chan?

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:04.210
Aoi-san?

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:08.860
I got the impression she's special to you.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:11.880
It's not quite that she's special.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.980
When she first came to my shop

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:15.590
and broke down crying about her breakup...

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:19.100
I felt like I was seeing my past self.

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:20.850
Your past self?

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:21.600
Yes.

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:25.350
But I didn't react the way she did.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:31.360
Seeing her cry, exposing all 
her weakness and ugliness...

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:35.360
I found it terribly admirable. 
Enviable, in a way.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:38.620
And so I wanted to help her.

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:40.870
O-Oh yeah?

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:45.520
Well, shall we have lunch, 
then head for the temple?

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:46.330
Sure!

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:51.880
Hey... lunch will be my treat, okay?

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.260
Let me pay, okay?

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.890
I really want to treat you!

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.270
I appreciate that.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:04.770
But I wish you wouldn't shout.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:14.370
Even if I have been put off women,

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:18.360
I would prefer to not have any 
misunderstandings about <i>our</i> relationship.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.710
Would you be Yagashira-san?

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:34.420
Yes.

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:36.260
A pleasure to meet you.

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:39.640
I am Ensho, a priest of Nanzenji Temple.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:42.560
Thank you for coming.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:46.180
You mentioned that you needed to talk to me.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:49.560
I'll allow the vice abbot to explain.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.810
Please, come this way.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.520
What does this say?

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:05.360
"Zuiryu."

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:07.830
It is the first title of Nanzenji's full name.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:09.770
As I'm sure you know,

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:19.220
<b>Zuiryu 
(Auspicious Dragon)</b>

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:14.640
this scroll was written by Nanzenji's 
eighth superintendent priest, Shimada Kikusen.

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:19.220
I see why you're known as the 
Holmes of Teramachi Sanjo.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:24.350
Oh, but I'm only known as Holmes 
because my surname is Yagashira.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.560
Now, don't be so humble.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.480
I've heard of your many great deeds.

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:30.800
It's hardly anything worth bragging about...

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:32.060
Oh, don't be like that.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:36.230
Would you like to have a 
look at our best pieces?

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.740
I certainly would.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:43.490
This is the national treasure, 
the old abbot's quarters.

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:47.350
The screen paintings are truly magnificent!

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:51.410
Yeah, this screen's totally dope!

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:54.000
Ah, I'm sorry...

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:56.030
Photography is not permitted here.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:59.630
But you can photograph that.

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:01.480
"Statue of Kanzan and Jittoku."

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:03.640
It's another of our temple's treasures.

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:06.140
It's magnificent!

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:10.390
It's just a statue of two old men cuddling.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.930
"Unryuzu" is another of your treasures, isn't it?

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:15.900
Yes, right this way.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:18.900
Hey, wait for me!

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:23.300
Hey, how'd you like that 
Zuiryu thing we saw before?

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.190
Oh, that?

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:28.160
I found it quite impressive.

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:29.790
Oh yeah?

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:34.410
I gotta say, this Ensho guy 
kinda has the same vibe you do.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:35.580
Does he?

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:38.050
You can't see it?

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:41.680
The way he walks... 
It's crazy similar to you.

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:44.400
Maybe you'd make a good priest.

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:47.120
I fear I'm brimming with too many worldly desires.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:53.340
It truly is magnificent!

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:58.440
This is what we wanted you 
to look at, Yagashira-san.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.940
"Unryuzu"? What's wrong with it?

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:04.320
I'll explain the rest in my room.

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:11.350
Greetings. I am the vice abbot, Unsho.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:14.330
My name is Shoan.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:18.970
Forgive us for calling you here
 on such short notice.

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:19.590
Not at all.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:22.090
How can I help you?

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:27.650
The truth is, the head abbot has been away 
on a study meeting for the last few days.

00:12:27.650 --> 00:12:34.610
After he left, Shoan found this letter at
 the feet of the "Statue of Kanzan and Jittoku."

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:37.480
If I may...

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:39.860
Residents of Nanzenji Temple:
I have taken the dragon.

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:43.610
"I've taken the dragon"?

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:48.580
For caution's sake, we looked at everything 
related to dragons in the temple,

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.990
but nothing was stolen.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:56.420
But if the letter was left at the feet 
of the "Statue of Kanzan and Jittoku"...

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:59.870
It's gotta be some nasty prank 
played by someone in the temple.

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:02.880
If it's not, it's gotta be
 breaking and entering.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:04.250
Indeed.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:08.600
We then heard that Seiji-san's 
grandson was quite a sharp young man,

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.640
so we decided to ask for your help.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:13.270
This letter was handwritten, wasn't it?

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:17.620
Could I see samples of handwriting 
from everyone in the temple?

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:25.280
I'll take a look now.

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:27.400
This one is mine.

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:29.030
Shoan's.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:30.660
Ensho's.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:34.900
This is another priest's.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:37.420
The last one is the head abbot's.

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:41.670
<i>Even I can tell this one...</i>

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:44.380
<i>The letter looks just like 
the abbot's handwriting!</i>

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:45.420
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.760
Thank you very much.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:51.930
I see now.

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:56.000
As the letter states,

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:59.940
Nanzenji Temple's precious 
"dragon" has already been stolen.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:01.940
Wh-What do you mean by that?

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:07.070
Rather than "stolen," perhaps it would be 
more accurate to say that it was "swapped."

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:08.970
Swapped?

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:10.950
You can't be serious...

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.250
Is that possible?

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:13.580
I don't know...

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:14.580
<i>Oh...</i>

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:16.680
<i>That's right...</i>

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:20.080
<i>There was just one treasure 
in the temple that Holmes saw</i>

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.840
<i>and didn't call "magnificent."</i>

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:25.630
<i>I found it quite impressive.</i>

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:28.130
<i>Is it possible...</i>

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:30.000
Your Zuiryu scroll.

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:32.010
It's a fake.

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:38.510
Kiyotaka-san, have you seen 
the Zuiryu scroll before?

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:39.140
Yes.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:41.400
But even putting that aside,

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:44.270
it was very clear to me that it was a fake.

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.400
What do you mean by that?

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:50.480
As my grandfather often says,
 "A fake is a fake;

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.180
it is not real."

00:14:53.310 --> 00:14:57.540
No matter how the maker may try, 
a fake always betrays a distinct intention...

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.540
The desire to deceive and mock others.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:02.670
An appraiser can sense that desire.

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:08.770
But we sometimes find fakes sophisticated
 enough to deceive an appraiser's eye

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:11.980
because they <i>weren't</i> made 
with the intent to deceive.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:13.800
The intent to deceive?

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.940
Yes. The forger enters a trance, 
envisions himself as the creator,

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:20.010
and copies the work.

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:23.420
The finished product then
contains no sense of malice.

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:26.250
The Zuiryu scroll is one such example.

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:28.290
But still, it is a fake,

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:30.880
so it lacks the aura that only 
the real work would give off.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:33.570
That's why you said it was impressive?

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:35.700
Vice Abbot.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:40.130
This temple is known for the fact that 
it once dealt with deceptive yokai.

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:44.830
I'm sorry to say that an impostor has 
come to dwell in Nanzenji once more.

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:46.960
An impostor?

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:48.210
Yes.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:48.960
Right here.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.470
My, my, my.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:16:00.210
You put on that charmin' countenance, 
but you've got such violence within.

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:02.230
Were you tryin' to split my head open?

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:07.360
I was hoping to stop right on 
the verge and intimidate you.

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:08.480
But you are impressive...

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:13.490
No kiddin'. I could sense the 
urge to strike miles away.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:16.990
So? When'd you figure it out?

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:21.000
The moment we first met, 
something seemed off.

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:24.620
For starters, you recognized me right away.

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:29.500
Of all the sightseers here, 
you picked me right out.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:33.880
And in front of the Zuiryu scroll, 
you seemed a little bit nervous.

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.480
You suddenly became loquacious,

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:39.760
and your breathing was a bit 
ragged during your explanation.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:44.140
Indeed, you are a copyist 
through and through.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:48.520
You naturally tend to take on the expressions
 and mannerisms of those around you.

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:53.540
I think you meant for the writing in the 
letter to look just like the head abbot's.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:55.660
Why would you go out of your way to do that?

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:01.160
I'd mastered the art of counterfeiting.

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:07.420
I got so good, nobody could 
tell my works were fakes.

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:13.920
At first it was excitin', 
but I got sick of it all real soon.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:17.180
So partly to atone for my crimes,

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:22.060
I forged a couple things and got 
myself accepted into the priesthood.

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:25.770
But early this spring, an old counterfeit 
dealer friend of mine said that

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:30.900
one of my Kizeto tea bowls had been 
exposed by a man even younger than me.

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:34.610
I learned he was so smart, 
people even called him "Holmes."

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:39.660
And suddenly, what I'd left behind
 started stirrin' in me all over again.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.790
You sought to produce counterfeits 
that could even fool museums?

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:46.410
I was hopin' to test you.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:50.170
That Zuiryu scroll's 
quite a work of art, ain't it?

00:17:50.390 --> 00:17:52.420
Don't you dare start callin' that art!

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:55.070
Counterfeits deceive people.

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:57.430
They ain't worthy of bein' called art!

00:17:57.920 --> 00:17:59.930
How dare you...

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:02.660
So that's the real you, eh?

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.870
Almost like a different person...

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:08.560
But I like it better than 
your prim-and-proper act.

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:11.160
Where's the real scroll?

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:12.820
In the temple storehouse.

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:17.740
Havin' someone like you around makes 
me think I still got ties to the world.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.950
Guess you beat me this time...

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:25.100
See ya!

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.290
Wait! You won't get away!

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:28.900
Wait!

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:29.960
What?

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:39.370
Kiyotaka-san, he's got the skills of a shinobi.

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:42.220
A pampered kid like you 
can't hope to catch him.

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:47.380
I beg your pardon, 
but I am not a pampered child.

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:49.330
You don't appear surprised by any of this...

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:51.730
Had you realized his true 
nature prior to this?

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:57.990
Yes. But it was our duty to accept 
Ensho's desire to join the priesthood.

00:18:58.590 --> 00:19:00.880
He'd forsaken his worldly ties
 and recited the Nenbutsu.

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:04.970
I think he was on the verge 
of becoming a true priest.

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.750
And that's when I saw through him?

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:12.180
I hurt his pride...

00:19:12.180 --> 00:19:16.000
But a the same time, 
I think it made Ensho happy.

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:22.870
Maybe after livin' in the shadows all this time, 
it felt like someone finally acknolwedged him.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:29.020
We couldn't fill the void in his spirit.

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:34.840
But maybe if you expose everything 
he's made and ruin him,

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:38.030
he'll find somethin' new beyond that.

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:44.530
Or perhaps his purpose in life
 is to be an object lesson for you.

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:48.040
We're leavin' Ensho in your hands...

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:50.660
Holmes-han of Teramachi Sanjo.

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:56.290
I see why you're the vice abbot of Nanzenji.

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:00.170
That's what happened?

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:04.600
Yeah! It was all like "bam!" 
It was crazy awesome!

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.430
Holmes is a real fighter!

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:10.430
"Fighter" is a crude way of putting it.

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:15.310
Ever since I was a child, my grandfather has 
demanded that I stay in shape. That's all.

00:20:15.680 --> 00:20:21.320
Since we would be buying expensive antiques
 in countries with poor security, you see.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.570
He wanted you to be his bodyguard?

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:24.770
Yes.

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:28.260
But, this Ensho-san...

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:29.830
What kind of person do you think he is?

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:31.580
Let me see...

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:34.530
From his appearance and conduct,

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:37.460
he seems emotionally unstable, 
with wild mood swings.

00:20:37.990 --> 00:20:41.840
But he's also a man with 
great confidence in himself.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:45.550
His emotional instability originated 
with experiences in his childhood.

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:49.720
His self-confidence stems 
from his natural talent.

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:53.480
Perhaps he's always been concerned 
with what others think of him.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.860
He may have spent his youth in poverty,

00:20:56.860 --> 00:21:01.360
exercising his talents in whatever 
way he had to to survive.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:06.740
And a close family member... 
his father, perhaps, was an artist.

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:10.660
Inspired by this person, 
Ensho pursued the path of art.

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:14.450
His father realized his talent and 
encouraged him to produce counterfeits.

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:18.190
But after perfecting his
 counterfeiting skills, he left home...

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:22.700
either because his closest family passed away,
 or because he was driven out.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:25.760
Is something the matter?

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:28.280
You really <i>are</i> Holmes.

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:29.890
I-I agree...

00:21:30.340 --> 00:21:31.650
Forgive me.

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:33.390
Aoi-san, here...

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:44.650
Ensho-san stole your fan, right?

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:48.330
Yes. If he's kept it rather 
than throwing it away,

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:50.660
I may have a chance to get it back someday.

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:54.790
I'm going to expose all of his work.

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:59.420
No matter what he counterfeits, 
I will expose it.

00:22:07.780 --> 00:22:13.700
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:23:37.720 --> 00:23:40.250
This is my first time at a party...

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:42.840
Aoi-san, anything you wear will suit you.

00:23:44.050 --> 00:23:46.700
Next Episode

00:23:44.050 --> 00:23:46.700
"The Connoisseur's Philosophy"

00:23:44.050 --> 00:23:46.700
Next time: "The Connoisseur's Philosophy."

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:49.000
Holmes-san, you really are nasty.
